WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.225
Rule twenty-eight is International only.

2
00:00:03.475 --> 00:00:13.675
A vessel constrained by her draft may show, in addition to her power-driven lights, three all-round red lights in a vertical line, or by day a cylinder.

3
00:00:13.925 --> 00:00:18.275
Rule twenty-nine covers pilot vessels on pilotage duty.

4
00:00:18.525 --> 00:00:22.950
She shows white over red all-round lights at or near the masthead.

5
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.575
White over red, pilot ahead.

6
00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:29.100
When underway she adds sidelights and a sternlight.

7
00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:32.250
At anchor she adds her anchor light or lights.

8
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:38.800
When a pilot vessel isn’t on pilotage duty, she shows the normal lights for a vessel of her length.
